<article class="env-lemma" id="B46142">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B46142">Lemma <span data-tag="B46142">5.4.5.3</span>.</a> Let $p: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a categorical fibration of $\infty $-categories, and let $f: K \rightarrow \calX $ be a diagram. Then the induced map $p': \calX _{f/} \rightarrow \calY _{p f/}$ is a categorical fibration. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It suffices to show that $p'$ has the right lifting property with respect to every inclusion $A \subseteq B$ which is a categorical equivalence. Unwinding the definitions, it suffices to show that $p$ has the right lifting property with respect to $i: K \star A \subseteq K \star B$. This is immediate, since $p$ is a categorical fibration and $i$ is a categorical equivalence. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>